 # The disk budget
 
+> **Native integration policy:** build-entry `disk-preflight` is a no-op. Builds do not
+> automatically delete caches or reserve disk space. Use `make disk` for inventory and coordinate
+> any scoped cleanup explicitly. The upstream planner/executor design below describes retained
+> optional tools; its automatic build-hook behavior is disabled in this integration.
+
 Build output is bounded by the tooling, not by briefing every agent to clean up after itself. This
 page is the design record of that tooling and the reference for the pieces that exist today:
 
